#: ../../run.md:22
msgid "Deploying a contract"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:24
msgid "To deploy a contract, it must first be compiled. There are three ways you can compile a contract:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:26
msgid "You can compile your contract directly from the {doc}`Solidity Compiler plugin </compile>`. This allows you to configure the compiler's behavior, including the Solidity version, optimization settings, and EVM target before compiling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:27
msgid "You can use the \"**Compile**\" button that appears in the main panel when you have an active Solidity file. The compilation uses the configuration from the Solidity Compiler plugin, applying whatever settings were last saved there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:28
msgid "You can compile directly from the Deploy & Run plugin using the \"Deploy\" section. It displays a list of the contracts active in the editor, along with a \"**Compile**\" button that compiles using the settings stored in the Solidity Compiler plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:30
msgid "![The Deploy tab showing the contract selector and Compile button.](images/deploy-and-run/deploy-tab.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:30
msgid "The Deploy tab showing the contract selector and Compile button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:32
msgid "Once you have compiled and selected your contract, choose the chain for deployment and/or method for deployment, deployment wallet, and EVM version in the **ENVIRONMENT** section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:34
msgid "![The Environment tab showing environment selector, account, gas limit, and value fields.](images/deploy-and-run/environment-tab.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:34
msgid "The Environment tab showing environment selector, account, gas limit, and value fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:37
msgid "If you want to connect Remix with a browser wallet (e.g., MetaMask, Phantom), set your environment to **Browser Extension** and choose your preferred wallet/chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:42
msgid "Before clicking **Deploy**, you can configure two additional fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:44
msgid "**Gas Limit**: Sets the maximum amount of gas allowed for the deployment transaction. Remix pre-fills a sensible default, but you can increase it if your contract is complex or if the deployment reverts due to an out-of-gas error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:45
msgid "**Value**: The amount of ETH (or WEI, Gwei, etc.) sent along with the deployment transaction. Only relevant if your contract has a payable constructor. Otherwise, leave it at 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:47
msgid "Clicking \"**Deploy**\" sends a transaction that deploys the selected contract. When the transaction is mined, the newly created instance will be added (this might take several seconds) to the \"**Deployed Contracts**\" section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:52
msgid "If the contract's constructor function has parameters, you will need to specify them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:55
msgid "Verifying on deployment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:56
msgid "When connected to a public network, there is a switch to enable contract verification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:58
msgid "![The contract verification switch.](images/deploy-and-run/deploy-verify-switch.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:58
msgid "The contract verification switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:60
msgid "The contract's source-code and metadata will be submitted to Etherscan, Sourcify, Blockscout, and Routescan.  For the verification to go through on Etherscan, their API needs to be input either in the Remix Settings panel or in the Contract Verification plugin's Settings tab.  Verification can also be done using the Contract Verification plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:62
msgid "Loading deployed contracts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:64
msgid "If a contract has already been deployed, you can load it into Remix using the \"**Add Contract**\" button on the **Deployed Contracts** section. Adding an already deployed contract costs no gas, since no redeployment is required. To load a deployed contract:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:67
msgid "Make sure the contract's source code or ABI is in the active tab of the Editor. If using source code, it must be compiled with the same settings as the originally deployed contract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:68
msgid "Enter the deployed contract's address in the contract address field that appears when you click the \"**Add Contract**\" button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:69
msgid "The contract instance will appear in the **Deployed Contracts** list, ready to interact with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:71
msgid "![The Deployed Contracts section showing the contract address field and Add button.](images/deploy-and-run/load-contract.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:71
msgid "The Deployed Contracts section showing the contract address field and Add button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:74
msgid "Only load contracts from addresses you trust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:77
msgid "Using the ABI to load contracts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:79
msgid "If you don't have the source code but have the contract's **ABI**, you can still load and interact with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:81
msgid "The ABI is a JSON array that describes a contract's functions, inputs, and outputs. To use it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:83
msgid "Create a new file in Remix with a `.abi` extension and paste the ABI content into it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:84
msgid "Make sure this file is the active tab in the Editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:85
msgid "Enter the contract address in the **Contract address** field and click the \"**Add**\" button. The contract will appear in the **Deployed Contracts** list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:88
msgid "To get the ABI of a contract you've compiled, open the Solidity Compiler plugin, compile the contract, then click **Compilation Details**. The ABI is listed in the modal that appears."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:91
msgid "Supported environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:93
msgid "The Deploy & Run plugin supports several environments that determine where your transactions are sent and how they are signed. You can choose between an in-browser sandbox (including forked chains), a browser wallet, a mobile wallet, or a locally running node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:95
msgid "Remix VM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:97
msgid "The Remix VM is a sandbox blockchain in the browser. Transactions do not require an approval to run. Remix VM comes with 10 accounts, each loaded with 100 ETH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:99
msgid "The Remix VM supports multiple EVM forks letting you simulate different network conditions without connecting to a live chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:101
msgid "The **state** of the Remix VM chain is saved in the **.states folder** in the File Explorer. If you do not want the Remix VM state to be saved, uncheck **Save environment state** in the Settings panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:103
msgid "Saving the state means you can refresh the browser and not lose your work, the caveat being that browser storage is inherently unstable. Pushing to a remote repository avoids relying on browser storage entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:107
msgid "In collaborative workflows, you can share the VM state by having teammates load the **state.json** file into their Remix instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:109
msgid "![The File Explorer showing the .states folder containing the state.json file.](images/deploy-and-run/a-deploy-run-state-file.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:109
msgid "The File Explorer showing the .states folder containing the state.json file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:111
msgid "Browser Extension"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:113
msgid "Browser extension wallets allow you to connect Remix to a wallet installed in your browser, such as **MetaMask** or **Phantom**. This is the standard way to deploy contracts to a live network or testnet using your own accounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:115
msgid "To use a browser extension:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:117
msgid "Install a supported wallet extension e.g., MetaMask. (This option will not be visible if you do not have an extension installed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:118
msgid "Set the **ENVIRONMENT** to **Browser Extension** in the Deploy & Run panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:120
msgid "Transactions sent through a browser extension require approval in the wallet popup before they are broadcast to the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:123
msgid "Make sure your wallet is unlocked and set to the correct network before deploying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:126
msgid "Mobile Wallets (Wallet Connect)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:128
msgid "WalletConnect allows you to connect Remix to a wallet on your mobile device by scanning a QR code. This is useful when you want to sign transactions with a hardware-backed or mobile wallet rather than a browser extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:130
msgid "To use WalletConnect:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:132
msgid "Set the **ENVIRONMENT** to **WalletConnect**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:133
msgid "A QR code will appear, scan it with your mobile wallet app (e.g., MetaMask Mobile, Rainbow, Trust Wallet)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:134
msgid "Approve the connection in your wallet. Remix will then use your mobile wallet's accounts and selected network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:136
msgid "Transactions triggered in Remix will appear as signing requests on your mobile device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:138
msgid "Development Environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:140
msgid "Development environments connect Remix to locally running nodes or L2 networks, making them suitable for advanced testing and integration workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:142
msgid "**Hardhat Provider**: Connects to a locally running [Hardhat](https://hardhat.org/) node. Transactions execute instantly and do not require wallet approval, making it fast for iterative development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:144
msgid "**Foundry Provider**: Connects to a locally running [Anvil](https://www.getfoundry.sh/anvil) node (part of the Foundry toolchain). Like Hardhat, it runs a local chain with pre-funded accounts and instant transaction finality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:146
msgid "**External HTTP Provider**: Connects Remix to any remote or local Ethereum-compatible node via an RPC URL (e.g., a Geth or Erigon instance). Enter the node's HTTP endpoint when prompted. Read more about [connecting to an External Provider](#more-about-external-http-provider)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:149
msgid "When using a local provider (Hardhat or Foundry), make sure the node is running before selecting the environment in Remix."
msgstr ""

