#: ../../run.md:184
msgid "Forking Chains in Remix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:186
msgid "Forking a chain will bring that chain to the Remix VM. Once it is forked, you'll have access to the 10 accounts loaded with 100 ETH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:188
msgid "Remix VM Forks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:190
msgid "You can also fork the Remix VM in its current state. To fork the Remix VM, click the version control icon to the right of the Environment title to create a fork and then to name it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:192
msgid "![Fork VM state modal.](images/deploy-and-run/fork-vm-state.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:192
msgid "Fork VM state modal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:194
msgid "You can switch between existing Remix VM forks by selecting \"Forked State\" from the Environment dropdown menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:196
msgid "![Forked state option.](images/deploy-and-run/forked-state.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:196
msgid "Forked state option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:199
msgid "The \"Forked State\" option only appears in the dropdown when there is an existing Remix VM fork."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:202
msgid "Live Network Forks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:204
msgid "The Remix VM can fork a live network, loading its state into the in-browser sandbox. This lets you test contracts against real on-chain data (such as existing token balances, deployed protocols, or mainnet contract state) without spending real ETH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:206
msgid "The following fork options are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:208
msgid "**Mainnet fork**: Forks the Ethereum mainnet at the latest block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:209
msgid "**Sepolia fork**: Forks the Sepolia testnet, useful for testing against testnet deployments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:210
msgid "**Custom fork**: Forks any EVM-compatible chain at a block number of your choice. See [Custom Fork](#forking-a-custom-chain) below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:212
msgid "Forking a Custom Chain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:214
msgid "The Custom fork option allows you to specify a chain's RPC server, a block number, and an EVM version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:216
msgid "![The Custom Fork modal showing fields for Node URL, block number, and EVM version.](images/deploy-and-run/custom-fork.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:216
msgid "The Custom Fork modal showing fields for Node URL, block number, and EVM version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:218
msgid "You can get the **Node URL** from [chainlist.org](https://chainlist.org). If the chain does not load, you may need to choose a different RPC server. You will also need to choose an EVM version appropriate to the block number. If you choose a very low block number, post-Merge EVM versions won't work since they didn't exist at that point in the chain's history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:220
msgid "You can reset the state of the VM by clicking the refresh icon to the right of the version control icon. Forking the VM lets you snapshot a working state, try changes, and return to the original if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:229
msgid "Using the recorder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:231
msgid "The Recorder is a tool used to save a sequence of transactions in a JSON file and re-run them later, either in the same environment or in another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:234
msgid "Saving to the JSON file (by default it's called scenario.json) allows one to easily check the transaction list, tweak input parameters, change linked libraries, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:236
msgid "There are many use cases for the Recorder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:238
msgid "For instance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:240
msgid "After having coded and tested contracts in a constrained environment, like the Remix VM, you could then switch the environment and redeploy the contract to a more realistic environment, like a public testnet or to a Geth node. By using the generated **scenario.json** file, you will be using all the same settings that you used in the Remix VM. The Recorder eliminates the need to manually recreate that state step by step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:243
msgid "You can also change the settings in the scenario.json file to customize the playback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:245
msgid "Deploying a contract often requires more than creating one transaction, and the Recorder will automate this deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:248
msgid "Working in a dev environment often requires setting up the state initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:251
msgid "![The Recorder panel showing the transactions recorded count and save button.](images/deploy-and-run/recorder.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:251
msgid "The Recorder panel showing the transactions recorded count and save button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:253
msgid "When checked, the option `Run transactions using the last compilation result` allows you to develop a contract and easily set the state using **the latest compiled versions of the contracts.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../run.md:255
msgid "scenario.json"
msgstr ""

